        "cited_text": "Most notable among these is Creative mode. In traditional Harness, the operating method was usually predetermined by product developers, and users could only choose from prepared configurations. Creative mode attempts to have the Agent itself understand the current runtime, test plugins according to the task, and combine the necessary capabilities. In other words, the configuration of Harness itself is beginning to become an object that the Agent can manipulate. How close this gets to a state where an \"Agent modifies its own Harness\" remains to be verified through future code, samples, and actual tasks. What can be confirmed at this point is that DeepSeek has opened up runtime reconfigurability to models, configuration files, and framework developers alike."
